.TH RADIUS 8 2026-11-23 "Peios radius 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
radius \- manage the Peios RADIUS service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B radius \-\-window
.br
.B radius
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I command
.RI [ argument ...]
.br
.B radius
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B radius
manages
.BR radiusd (8):
its clients, access policies, authentication profiles, server identities, assignment and accounting, and the service itself.
.B radius \-\-window
opens the RADIUS window, for the GXWI desktop, which does the same.
.PP
Configuration is kept in the Registry under
.BR Machine\eSoftware\eRadius ,
and
.B radius
writes it directly, as the person running it, so it can do exactly what that person may, and works while
.B radiusd
is stopped.
Saving a change doesn't mean
.B radiusd
has taken it up:
.B radius status
shows the saved and the effective configuration apart.
.PP
Every object has a GUID that never changes, and a name that is only a label: names can be changed, and repeated, so a name that is ambiguous has to be given as its GUID.
References between objects are always GUIDs.
.B radius
refuses to delete an object another refers to, and names the ones that do.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
The service's state, and the saved and effective configuration.
.TP
.BR "config init" | show | check
.B init
creates an absent configuration: an empty one, which admits nobody, with a UDP listener at
.BR 0.0.0.0:1812 ,
and the protected directory
.I /var/state/radius/credentials
for credential files.
It refuses a machine that has a configuration.
.B show
prints the configuration and
.B check
validates it.
.TP
.BI "config set " NAME = VALUE " ..."
Change global settings.
.TP
.BI "client" "|policy|profile|identity|access\-profile|rule|..." " list"
List the objects of a kind.
The kinds are
.BR client ,
.BR policy " (access policy),"
.BR profile " (authentication profile),"
.BR identity " (server identity),"
.BR access\-profile ,
.BR rule " (assignment rule),"
.BR dynamic\-profile " (session control profile),"
.B quota
and
.BR accounting\-profile .
.TP
.IB kind " show " name-or-guid
Show an object.
.TP
.IB kind " create " name " \fR[\fB\-\-set \fIfield\fB=\fIvalue\fR] ..."
.TQ
.IB kind " set " name-or-guid " \fR[\fB\-\-set \fIfield\fB=\fIvalue\fR] ..."
.TQ
.IB kind " unset " name-or-guid " " field " ..."
.TQ
.IB kind " delete " name-or-guid
Create, change and delete objects.
Lists are comma-separated.
.TP
.IB kind " enable" | "disable " name-or-guid
Enable or disable a client, policy or profile.
A disabled one denies what it would have admitted, without falling back to another.
.TP
.IB kind " permissions " name-or-guid " connect" | "management \fR[\fIsddl\fR]"
Show or set who may connect through an access policy, or manage an object.
.TP
.BI "client secret " name-or-guid " show" | generate | "set \fR[\fB\-\-stdin\fR | \fB\-\-file \fIpath\fR]"
Show, generate or set a client's shared secret.
.B set
without an input option prompts without echo.
.TP
.BI "identity import " name-or-guid " \-\-set CertificateFiles=" path ",... \-\-set PrivateKeyFile=" path
.TQ
.BI "identity inspect " name-or-guid
Import a server identity's certificate chain and private key, in PEM or DER, checking that they match, or show its names, issuer, expiry and fingerprint.
.TP
.BI "policy explain " name-or-guid " \-\-facts " path
Explain what the saved policy would do for hypothetical facts, given as typed JSON.
.TP
.B access\-profile fields
.TQ
.B dynamic\-profile template wispr
List the typed settings and standard attributes an access profile may set, or print a session control profile with WISPr rate mappings.
.TP
.BR "accounting init" | telemetry\-init | status | "sessions \fR[\fIpolicy-guid\fR]"
Create the private accounting ledger directory, or the service's metric namespace; show accounting's state; list sessions.
.TP
.BR "accounting session" | history | related | commands | reconciliation " \fIsession-guid"
Show a session, its history, the sessions related to it, the commands sent for it, or how its records were reconciled.
.TP
.BR "accounting disconnect" | reauthenticate | "update \fIsession-guid\fR [\fB\-\-request\-id \fIid\fR]"
Send a Disconnect or Change-of-Authorization request for a session.
Each needs its own right in the accounting security descriptor.
.TP
.BR "accounting usage \fIsid\fR [\fIpolicy-guid\fR]"
A person's usage.
.TP
.BI "accounting annotate " "session-guid note"
.TQ
.BI "accounting correct\-end " "session-guid unix-milliseconds note " \-\-confirm
Add a note to a session, or correct when it ended, with the reason.
.TP
.B accounting rebuild \-\-confirm
Rebuild the retained accounting evidence, without sending any session controls.
.TP
.BR "diagnostics list" | follow " \fR[\fB\-\-since \fIseconds\fR] [\fIfilters\fR]"
.TQ
.BI "diagnostics show " attempt-id
.TQ
.BR "diagnostics drops" | status
Read
.BR radiusd 's
record of authentication attempts from the event store, which needs
.BR eventd (8).
.TP
.BR "service start" | stop | restart
Start, stop or restart
.BR radiusd .
Stopping it interrupts authentication; stations already connected keep their access until they reauthenticate.
.TP
.BR "service boot on" | off
Have
.B radiusd
start at boot, or not, without starting or stopping it now.
The radius package leaves automatic startup disabled.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the result, or the error, as JSON, with GUIDs and typed error codes.
A secret shown by
.B client secret show
is printed raw, and doesn't take
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-window
Open the RADIUS window.
.SH SETTING UP
.nf
.B radius config init
.BI "radius identity create Main \-\-set CertificateFiles=" chain.pem " \e"
.BI "    \-\-set PrivateKeyFile=" server.key
.BI "radius profile create Passwords \-\-set AuthenticationMethods=peap\-mschapv2,ttls\-pap \e"
.BI "    \-\-set ServerIdentity=" identity-guid
.BI "radius policy create Household \-\-set SSID=Home \e"
.BI "    \-\-set AuthenticationProfile=" profile-guid " \e"
.BI "    \-\-set 'ConnectSecurity=O:SYG:SYD:(A;;0x1;;;" group-sid ")'"
.BI "radius client create AccessPoints \-\-set Addresses=10.10.0.0/16 \-\-set Policies=" policy-guid
.B radius service boot on
.B radius service start
.fi
.PP
Replace the placeholder GUIDs and group SID with actual values.
The client receives a generated shared secret; reveal it with
.B radius client secret AccessPoints show
and configure the access point with the same secret.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Any other failure.
.TP
.B 3
Permission was denied.
.TP
.B 4
An object was not found.
.TP
.B 5
The configuration is not valid.
.TP
.B 64
An argument was not valid.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR regman (1),
.BR radiusd (8)
.PP
https://learn.peios.org/peios/reference/radius/administration
